# CONTROLLER CONVENTIONS – SmartCartPro

## 1. Endpoint XML comments
- Add a concise `/// <summary>` (max **two** prose lines) above every public action.
- State business purpose and when/who uses it. No obvious implementation noise.
- Do not document private properties or constructors.

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Displays the current platform license details and defaults when none exists.
/// Used by the Platform Super Admin to view and manage license settings.
/// </summary>
[HttpGet]
public async Task<IActionResult> Index(CancellationToken ct)
```

## 2. View → Input mapping
- After `CommonHelpers.ValidateModelState(ModelState)` (when used), build `var input = new Input… { … };` then call the service.
- Preserve ActorUserId, enum ints, null-coalesce, nested line collections, and other existing transforms in that initializer.
- Route-id Select/List inputs (`new InputXSelect { Id = id }`) may stay compact on GET helpers.

## 3. Responses
- Mutating AJAX success → `CommonHelpers.SuccessResponse(…)` → `CommonResponseModel`.
- Failures → throw typed `AppException` (handler returns `CommonResponseModel` for JSON paths).
- Do not invent one-off path hardcodes in `ExceptionErrorMapper`; use general conventions (`*Json` actions, XHR, Accept, mutating MVC prefixes).
